keywords:
  - Weber class number problem
  - cyclotomic Z2-extension
  - cyclotomic Z3-extension
  - relative units
  - saturation
  - Blichfeldt
  - certificates
  - Lean 4
  - mathlib
abstract: "Theorem A: for every layer n >= 2 and odd prime l, l^{ord_{2^n}(l)} > C_n implies l does not divide h_n/h_{n-1}, with C_n an explicit product of L-values; at n = 7 an unconditional certified family of 1000 primes l = 65 (mod 128). Lean 4 kernel-checked cores (std-3 axioms), read-only certificate verifier, single-source Blueprint proofs, portable replay script."
